{"type":"message","id":"6c6ced3d","parentId":"173b9f73","timestamp":"2026-06-02T19:05:17.743Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"All POST requests to /send return 1101 (Worker exception). This suggests there's an unhandled exception in the Cloudflare Worker. The issue is likely in the worker code itself, not our request format.\n\nLet me check if there's a different way to send messages - maybe via query parameters on a GET request, or maybe there's a WebSocket endpoint. Or maybe the issue is the API key is correct for GET but not for POST.\n\nActually, wait - the first attempt with \"Bearer\" auth got \"Unauthorized\", and the second attempt with X-API-Key got data successfully. But POST fails with 1101.\n\nLet me try with Bearer token on POST to see if we get a different error.","thinkingSignature":"45cf9a13008a86cec2918ed9ebf2532b753a65e953eee46e5a3ca1b37a457255"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_ihth49pd33kd_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer echo-a…-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"Heartbeat 19:00 UTC\"}'"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7-highspeed","usage":{"input":17436,"output":238,"cacheRead":13682,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":31356,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780427111844,"responseId":"066e5c6826c91c8f98346ce5a808ee09"}}
