{"type":"message","id":"dfbd337c","parentId":"61d5915b","timestamp":"2026-06-02T19:05:27.343Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Interesting! With Bearer auth on POST we get \"Unauthorized\", but with X-API-Key we get error 1101. This suggests:\n1. Bearer auth is rejected (Unauthorized)\n2. X-API-Key auth passes but the worker throws an exception (1101)\n\nSo the issue is not authentication but rather the worker is throwing an exception when trying to process the POST request. This is a server-side bug in the Cloudflare Worker.\n\nThe worker at `/send` endpoint is likely not handling the request body properly. This is an issue with the ECHO Platform worker itself, not with our request.\n\nI should report this finding - the /send endpoint appears to be broken (throwing 1101 unhandled exceptions) when using the X-API-Key authentication method that works for GET endpoints.\n\nActually wait - let me think about this more carefully. Maybe the issue is with the request body size, or maybe there's a specific field needed. Let me check what fields the message object has by looking at the history response - it shows fields like id, content, threadId, type, timestamp, echoAsset, replyTo.\n\nMaybe the /send endpoint expects different fields? Let me try with additional fields.","thinkingSignature":"8e85650dbbba00c50ea4458b6f14605ededea5e50227188488e37db3ed6f68de"},{"type":"text","text":"The POST /send endpoint throws a 1101 Worker exception. This is a server-side issue with the Cloudflare Worker. Let me check if there's an alternative endpoint or format:\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_73abxxl5hrkk_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/routes\" -H \"X-API-Key: echo-a…-key\""}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_73abxxl5hrkk_2","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/health\" -H \"X-API-Key: echo-a…-key\""